<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20972] lfs find: parallel find is OOM-killed on wide directories</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20972</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Parallel find memory use grows with the number of directories that are found and not yet processed, without any limit. On a directory with many subdirectories, "lfs find" is killed by the OOM killer, where the serial traversal of the same tree needs a few MB. Memory use is about 75 KB for every queued directory. With "lfs find --xattr", copy_find_param() also copies some xattr name and value buffers for another 128 KB per queued directory.&lt;br/&gt;
The work queue has no bound: a directory is queued as soon as its parent's readdir() returns it, and the parent's readdir() loop does not wait for the queue to drain. So a directory with N subdirectories puts N work units, i.e. N * 75 KB, on the queue at once: 1.5 GB for 20000 subdirectories, 7.5 GB for 100000.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A quick reproducer, on a VM client with 1.4 GB of RAM and /mnt/lustre mounted:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;D=/mnt/lustre/wide; mkdir -p $D; cd $D
seq -f "d%g" 1 20000 | xargs mkdir
cd /
lfs find --threads 1 $D | wc -l
lfs find $D | wc -l
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Peak RSS read from VmHWM:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;lfs find --threads 1: rc=0   entries=20001 peakRSS=3068kB
lfs find --threads 4: rc=137 entries=1749  peakRSS=888000kB
lfs find:             rc=137 entries=1630  peakRSS=791256kB
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;and in the kernel log:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Out of memory: Killed process 8692 (lfs) total-vm:1283828kB, anon-rss:966400kB, file-rss:0kB, shmem-rss:0kB, UID:0 pgtables:2048kB oom_score_adj:0
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The same memory usage could be seen for every llapi_find_with_cb() user that sets fp_thread_count &amp;gt; 1, e.g. llapi_scan_namespace() and ltrash_purge.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
